__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
# Licensed market data must never be committed. EODHD and similar vendors
# license data for your own use, not for redistribution -- and a GitHub repo is
# redistribution.
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing: a bare `data/` matches ANY directory named
# data at any depth, which silently excluded src/tradelab/data/ and left the
# EODHD provider untracked. Anchor it to the repository root.
/data/
*.parquet
*.csv
*.duckdb
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
# Operational state is ignored EXCEPT the paper-trading track record, which is
# committed deliberately: the container running it is wiped between sessions,
# and version history makes the record auditable -- a result cannot be quietly
# revised after the fact.
state/*
logs/
*.log
runs/
research/output/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
secrets.yaml
.eodhd_token
*.token

# The paper-trading track record is committed deliberately: the container it
# runs in is wiped between sessions, and version history makes the record
# auditable -- a published result cannot be quietly revised afterwards.
#
# Two gitignore subtleties, both of which silently defeated earlier attempts:
#   - `state/*` not `state/`, because git never descends into an excluded
#     directory, so a negation beneath one is never reached.
#   - These negations must come LAST, after `*.sqlite` above, since later
#     rules win.
!state/paper/
!state/paper/*.json
!state/paper/*.sqlite

# Broker credentials. Never committed.
deploy/.env
